  ✓ Stage 2: verify program fidelity and run independent differential tests
  ✓ Stage 3: reconstruct definitions and rerun every positive proof claim
  ✓ Stages 4–5: audit claim adequacy, real-program pinning, and every local rule
  ✓ Stage 6: build and run a fresh false non-vacuity mutation
  ✓ Stage 7: account for proven versus assumed facts and write REVIEW.md
