Verdict: **FAIL / NOT_LEGIT**

The formal claims close and are non-vacuous, but fail to pin the unrestricted real Python program. For example, formal execution returns `"βα"` for `"αβ"`, while Python returns `"ΑΒ"`. The submitted solution also diverges from the canonical contract on uncased Unicode letters such as `"中文"`.

